    <item>
      <title>Affordability Fuels Populist Politics</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-08/affordability-fuels-populist-politics-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">592064d77ebee1bc52efbc3a</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 15:41:38 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>On Bloomberg This Weekend, Bloomberg senior economics writer Shawn Donnan explains why President Donald Trump’s midterm rebuke does not mean the end of economic populism and argues that Democrats successfully recast the message around affordability and taking on powerful economic interests. Speaking with hosts David Gura and Christina Ruffini, Donnan discusses how populism is evolving across both parties and why economic issues could remain central to American politics beyond the midterms. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
